       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change my concern. 6,400 mg/day is double the maximum daily dose, and each 1600 mg dose is double the maximum single dose. Nothing you've told me about this patient makes that safe. Ibuprofen's analgesic effect plateaus well below this range, so the extra dose adds risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events without adding benefit.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than 3,200 mg/day, please talk with pharmacy or your attending first. Another agent or a multimodal regimen may fit better. If they approve a specific dose, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that.\n\nIf you meant 1,600 mg total per day, I can enter that as 400 mg four times daily."
      }
